    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Spending time in space sounds exciting. But it can be hard on the human body. Without gravity, everything changes: Muscles get weaker, bones lose strength, blood rushes to the head, and even simple movements become difficult. That’s why scientists need to find ways to protect astronauts before they travel to the Moon or Mars."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "To study this, ten healthy men volunteered for a special experiment in France. They agreed to spend ten days lying flat in a lab. For their time, each earned $5,500. The men had to be between 20 and 40 years old, and between 1.65 and 1.77 metres tall. They also had to have no "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "allergies",
            "ref": "v-allergy"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or special diets."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The volunteers lay in bathtub-like containers filled with water. A "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "waterproof cover",
            "zh": "防水盖"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " kept them dry. They floated in the water up to their chests, with only their heads and arms out of the water. It looked like floating on invisible clouds. The waterbeds copied the weightlessness of space. Even the simplest tasks became challenging. The men ate meals while lying flat, with trays floating on boards. Going to the bathroom was also difficult. The volunteers had to remain flat while being rolled away on a trolley!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "These experiences are part of a method called "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "dry immersion",
            "zh": "干浸法"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It’s a cheaper and simpler way to study how the body reacts to weightlessness. It causes blood to rush to the head, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "body fluids",
            "zh": "体液"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to shift, and muscles and bones to weaken—just like in space."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "After ten days, the men stayed five more days for medical tests. They returned ten days later for a final check-up. Scientists carefully "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "observed",
            "ref": "v-observe"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " how their bodies adjusted to normal life again. The results will help astronauts survive long space missions and may also help people on Earth. This research could improve care for "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bedridden patients",
            "zh": "卧床患者"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", the elderly, and those with "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "mobility problems",
            "zh": "活动困难"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Bridging space research and Earth medicine is very important,” said Marc-Antoine Custaud, who led the study. “Our findings may help both astronauts and people on Earth.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
